# ===========================================================================
# What this repository tracks
#
# Only what is needed to RUN the system and READ the work: run.py, src/,
# the three required input datasets, the docs, the paper, and the generated
# outputs. Everything excluded below still exists locally - it is kept off
# GitHub because nothing in the live pipeline reads it.
# ===========================================================================

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Superseded material -----------------------------------------------------
# Datasets and artefacts from earlier revisions of the project. README.md says
# it plainly: nothing live reads these. ~10 MB of embeddings and retired CSVs.
archive/

# Notebooks retired in PROJECT.md rev 3 (embedding and global-cost-matrix
# approaches, both abandoned). Kept locally as a record of what was tried.
codes/

# Reference PDFs and earlier drafts (~3 MB). Third-party papers should not be
# redistributed, and they are not needed to run or review the system.
docs/

# --- Large inputs the pipeline does not require ------------------------------
# The raw 86k-review corpus (14 MB). It is OPTIONAL: only
# sentiment_build.audit_leakage() would use it, and the delivered sentiment
# dataset already carries the reviews and ratings it needs for that test.
employee_reviews.csv

# Duplicate delivery. Byte-identical to the Capgemini file (verified: only the
# CSV dtype of the rating columns differs) and saved under a broken filename.
dataset/datasetsentiment_fuzzy.csv

# --- Trained model artefacts -------------------------------------------------
# The sentiment notebook is reference-only and the scores are delivered to us
# as a dataset, so a local checkpoint is never needed here.
neurofuzzy_bert_saved/

# --- LaTeX build products (the PDF is compiled on Overleaf) ------------------
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.pdf
!paper/results/*.pdf

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
